WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.645
<v Examiner>The closed questions.

2
00:00:02.645 --> 00:00:05.762
<v Examiner>The facts her quizzes ask that no other track covers.

3
00:00:06.212 --> 00:00:10.731
About seventy per cent of Test 3's marks are closed questions: multiple choice,

4
00:00:10.731 --> 00:00:13.363
true or false, drop-downs and matching tables.

5
00:00:13.363 --> 00:00:16.910
Most tracks in this episode are built around a written answer,

6
00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.369
and each section ended with its fine print.

7
00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:23.088
This one picks up the rest: the one-line facts her quiz keys ask,

8
00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:27.035
most of them in two different quizzes, that no written answer covers.

9
00:00:27.035 --> 00:00:30.468
A few of them sit outside her checklist, like fertilisation,

10
00:00:30.468 --> 00:00:32.298
but her quizzes ask them anyway.

11
00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:33.156
No essays here.

12
00:00:33.156 --> 00:00:35.673
Just the fact, and the wording her key uses.

13
00:00:36.123 --> 00:00:38.126
The hook: dark room, big pupils.

14
00:00:38.126 --> 00:00:39.941
Gentamicin breaks hair cells.

15
00:00:39.941 --> 00:00:43.697
And the corpus luteum makes three hormones for three months.

16
00:00:44.147 --> 00:00:45.779
Genetics first, two facts.

17
00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:49.860
The chromosome conditions, the way her matching table pairs them.

18
00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.121
Down syndrome is trisomy twenty-one.

19
00:00:52.121 --> 00:00:54.444
Edwards syndrome is trisomy eighteen.

20
00:00:54.444 --> 00:00:59.028
Turner syndrome is a woman with only one X chromosome, forty-five in all,

21
00:00:59.028 --> 00:01:02.858
with underdeveloped female characteristics and a webbed neck.

22
00:01:02.858 --> 00:01:07.755
Klinefelter syndrome is a man with one Y and two or more X chromosomes, X X Y,

23
00:01:07.755 --> 00:01:11.585
forty-seven in all, with underdeveloped male characteristics.

24
00:01:11.585 --> 00:01:15.792
On a karyotype picture, Klinefelter is the one with a Y and two Xs.

25
00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:18.429
She shows you that picture in two quizzes.

26
00:01:18.879 --> 00:01:20.133
And fetal testing.

27
00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:25.706
Her key, in two quizzes: the most common form of fetal testing is amniocentesis.

28
00:01:27.156 --> 00:01:27.625
The eye.

29
00:01:27.625 --> 00:01:29.148
First, the pupil's nerves.

30
00:01:29.148 --> 00:01:32.078
When you walk into a dark room, the pupils dilate,

31
00:01:32.078 --> 00:01:36.707
because the radial muscles of the iris contract, under sympathetic stimulation.

32
00:01:36.707 --> 00:01:41.981
In bright light, and for near vision, the pupils constrict: the circular muscles contract,

33
00:01:41.981 --> 00:01:43.973
under parasympathetic stimulation.

34
00:01:43.973 --> 00:01:45.614
So sympathetic means dilate,

35
00:01:45.614 --> 00:01:50.067
and her key adds that sympathetic is more predominant during distant vision.

36
00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:53.524
Think of being scared in the dark: sympathetic, big pupils.

37
00:01:53.974 --> 00:01:56.292
The image, the way her drop-down runs.

38
00:01:56.292 --> 00:01:57.574
The lens is biconvex.

39
00:01:57.574 --> 00:02:01.356
So the image on the retina is real, and inverted: upside down.

40
00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:04.773
Through experience, the brain learns to turn it upright.

41
00:02:04.773 --> 00:02:07.214
The optic nerves form the optic chiasma,

42
00:02:07.214 --> 00:02:12.034
where half of the fibres from each eye cross to the opposite side of the brain.

43
00:02:12.034 --> 00:02:17.098
And the images from the two eyes are combined when the two halves of the brain talk

44
00:02:17.098 --> 00:02:18.806
through the corpus callosum.

45
00:02:19.256 --> 00:02:20.700
Three one-mark words.

46
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.762
The eyelids are the palpebrae.

47
00:02:22.762 --> 00:02:24.824
Lacrimal secretions are tears.

48
00:02:24.824 --> 00:02:29.155
And pinkeye is an infection of the conjunctiva: conjunctivitis.

49
00:02:30.605 --> 00:02:33.873
Her eye-conditions matching table is twelve marks,

50
00:02:33.873 --> 00:02:37.076
and it names five conditions no other track does.

51
00:02:37.076 --> 00:02:41.651
Blepharitis: inflammation of the tiny oil glands of the inner eyelids.

52
00:02:41.651 --> 00:02:46.815
Diabetic retinopathy: damage to the blood vessels of the retina, with floaters,

53
00:02:46.815 --> 00:02:50.148
blurriness, dark areas, and trouble seeing colours.

54
00:02:50.148 --> 00:02:54.528
Retinitis pigmentosa: hereditary, and the rods are destroyed first,

55
00:02:54.528 --> 00:02:56.946
so night blindness is the early sign.

56
00:02:56.946 --> 00:03:01.979
Dry macular degeneration: drusen build up between the choroid and the retina,

57
00:03:01.979 --> 00:03:04.332
and central vision blurs or is lost.

58
00:03:04.332 --> 00:03:09.169
Wet macular degeneration: the same, plus blood leaking out of the vessels.

59
00:03:09.169 --> 00:03:14.267
And her true or false: diabetes can cause cataracts, glaucoma and retinopathy.

60
00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:14.594
True.

61
00:03:15.044 --> 00:03:16.769
Then her treatments table.

62
00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:21.414
Glaucoma: beta blockers, which slow down the making of aqueous humour.

63
00:03:21.414 --> 00:03:24.533
Conjunctivitis: the antibiotic chloramphenicol.

64
00:03:24.533 --> 00:03:27.917
Astigmatism: toric lenses, or rigid contact lenses.

65
00:03:27.917 --> 00:03:32.563
Retinal detachment: laser surgery, making small burns around the area.

66
00:03:32.563 --> 00:03:36.544
Cataract: surgery to remove the clouded lens and replace it.

67
00:03:36.544 --> 00:03:40.857
And dry macular degeneration: there's no effective treatment yet.

68
00:03:42.307 --> 00:03:42.828
The ear.

69
00:03:42.828 --> 00:03:43.805
Ototoxic drugs.

70
00:03:43.805 --> 00:03:48.950
Her help board files hearing loss from certain medications under sensorineural.

71
00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.294
Ototoxic means poisonous to the ear:

72
00:03:51.294 --> 00:03:54.941
these drugs damage the hair cells of the organ of Corti.

73
00:03:54.941 --> 00:03:59.370
Her list: aminoglycoside antibiotics like gentamicin, some TB drugs,

74
00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:04.775
the chemotherapy drug cisplatin, loop diuretics like furosemide, high-dose aspirin,

75
00:04:04.775 --> 00:04:05.556
and quinine.

76
00:04:05.556 --> 00:04:10.440
So her true or false, that gentamicin causes conduction deafness, is false:

77
00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.678
it's sensorineural.

78
00:04:11.678 --> 00:04:15.129
And when she lists causes of conductive hearing loss,

79
00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:18.190
ototoxic drugs are the one that doesn't belong.

80
00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.127
Pitch along the cochlea.

81
00:04:20.127 --> 00:04:23.783
The basilar membrane changes in stiffness along its length,

82
00:04:23.783 --> 00:04:26.447
so each part answers a different frequency.

83
00:04:26.447 --> 00:04:30.474
High frequencies are picked up at the base, near the oval window.

84
00:04:30.474 --> 00:04:34.192
Low frequencies are picked up furthest from the oval window.

85
00:04:34.642 --> 00:04:35.467
Sound shirts.

86
00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:40.545
Deaf people can feel music, because loud sound waves are vibrations of a medium,

87
00:04:40.545 --> 00:04:44.925
including our own tissues, and they're picked up by mechanoreceptors.

88
00:04:45.375 --> 00:04:50.226
The Doppler effect: a change in the frequency, or the wavelength, of a wave,

89
00:04:50.226 --> 00:04:53.163
for an observer moving relative to its source.

90
00:04:53.163 --> 00:04:57.695
Her example: a siren sounds higher as the police car comes towards you,

91
00:04:57.695 --> 00:04:59.483
and lower as it drives away.

92
00:04:59.483 --> 00:05:02.100
Sitting in the car, you'd hear no change.

93
00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:05.961
Last, fertilisation and early pregnancy.

94
00:05:05.961 --> 00:05:10.782
They aren't on her checklist, but her quizzes ask them, so they're worth having.

95
00:05:11.232 --> 00:05:12.797
Her fertilisation drop-down.

96
00:05:12.797 --> 00:05:16.151
On the way to the egg, the number of sperm falls a long way,

97
00:05:16.151 --> 00:05:19.617
but a male immune attack on the egg is not one of the reasons.

98
00:05:19.617 --> 00:05:23.306
That's the option to pick when she asks which one is NOT a reason.

99
00:05:23.306 --> 00:05:25.766
The egg is fertilised in the fallopian tube.

100
00:05:25.766 --> 00:05:29.343
The outer layer covering the egg, which comes from the follicle,

101
00:05:29.343 --> 00:05:31.076
her key calls the zona radiata.

102
00:05:31.076 --> 00:05:32.082
Pick that wording.

103
00:05:32.082 --> 00:05:34.262
Her figures call it the corona radiata,

104
00:05:34.262 --> 00:05:37.616
and the zona pellucida is the wrong option in that question.

105
00:05:37.616 --> 00:05:42.144
And the mineral the sperm needs to get through the egg's outer layers is calcium.

106
00:05:42.594 --> 00:05:48.343
When conception is most likely: around ovulation, days ten to seventeen of the cycle.

107
00:05:48.343 --> 00:05:53.822
An ovulation predictor kit works by picking up the sharp peak of LH in the urine,

108
00:05:53.822 --> 00:05:55.310
just before ovulation.

109
00:05:55.310 --> 00:06:00.045
Her hormone tables add that oestrogen peaks just before ovulation too,

110
00:06:00.045 --> 00:06:03.630
and it's oestrogen that stimulates the release of LH.

111
00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.591
FSH makes the follicles grow.

112
00:06:07.041 --> 00:06:10.153
After fertilisation, the corpus luteum keeps going.

113
00:06:10.153 --> 00:06:15.582
For the first three months of pregnancy it makes three hormones: progesterone, oestrogen,

114
00:06:15.582 --> 00:06:16.314
and relaxin.

115
00:06:16.314 --> 00:06:18.999
After three months, the placenta takes over.

116
00:06:18.999 --> 00:06:22.415
If there's no pregnancy, it becomes the corpus albicans.

117
00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:27.052
So on her hormone graph, pregnancy removes the drop at about day twenty-one:

118
00:06:27.052 --> 00:06:29.431
oestrogen and progesterone keep rising.

119
00:06:29.431 --> 00:06:33.274
A pregnancy test looks for human chorionic gonadotropin, H C G.

120
00:06:33.274 --> 00:06:37.484
And the baby is an embryo up to eight weeks, and a foetus after that.

121
00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:40.208
Contraception, her matching table.

122
00:06:40.208 --> 00:06:43.085
Condoms are a barrier that keeps semen out.

123
00:06:43.085 --> 00:06:45.359
An I U D may prevent implantation.

124
00:06:45.359 --> 00:06:48.370
Hormonal contraception may prevent ovulation.

125
00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:51.447
And the mini pill, the progesterone-only pill:

126
00:06:51.447 --> 00:06:54.925
it thickens the cervical mucus and thins the lining,

127
00:06:54.925 --> 00:06:59.006
but it does not release oxytocin or make the uterus contract.

128
00:06:59.006 --> 00:07:00.611
That's her wrong option.

129
00:07:01.061 --> 00:07:02.755
Breast cancer, from her key.

130
00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:07.653
The risk factors are all of these: no breastfeeding, or only short periods of it;

131
00:07:07.653 --> 00:07:11.100
early periods and a late menopause; and a family history.

132
00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:16.421
And men can get breast cancer too, so they should check their breasts for lumps as well.

133
00:07:17.871 --> 00:07:18.549
The traps.

134
00:07:18.549 --> 00:07:21.801
Sympathetic dilates, parasympathetic constricts.

135
00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:26.001
Ototoxic drugs cause sensorineural deafness, never conduction.

136
00:07:26.001 --> 00:07:30.133
High pitch is at the base of the cochlea, by the oval window.

137
00:07:30.133 --> 00:07:32.775
Klinefelter is the man with an extra X.

138
00:07:32.775 --> 00:07:35.214
Turner is the woman with only one X.

139
00:07:35.214 --> 00:07:40.634
And the corpus luteum's three hormones are progesterone, oestrogen, and relaxin.

140
00:07:41.084 --> 00:07:41.667
<v Examiner>Once more.

141
00:07:41.667 --> 00:07:43.708
<v Examiner>The facts her closed questions ask.

142
00:07:46.158 --> 00:07:50.191
Down syndrome is trisomy twenty-one, Edwards trisomy eighteen.

143
00:07:50.191 --> 00:07:52.729
Turner: a woman with one X, forty-five.

144
00:07:52.729 --> 00:07:55.526
Klinefelter: a man with X X Y, forty-seven.

145
00:07:55.526 --> 00:07:58.388
The most common fetal test is amniocentesis.

146
00:07:58.388 --> 00:08:02.292
In the dark, the pupils dilate: radial muscles, sympathetic.

147
00:08:02.292 --> 00:08:07.626
In bright light and near vision they constrict: circular muscles, parasympathetic.

148
00:08:07.626 --> 00:08:11.074
The lens is biconvex, the image is real and inverted,

149
00:08:11.074 --> 00:08:13.872
half the fibres cross at the optic chiasma,

150
00:08:13.872 --> 00:08:16.994
and the corpus callosum combines the two images.

151
00:08:16.994 --> 00:08:20.963
The eyelids are the palpebrae, lacrimal secretions are tears,

152
00:08:20.963 --> 00:08:22.979
and pinkeye is the conjunctiva.

153
00:08:23.429 --> 00:08:26.759
Blepharitis is inflamed oil glands in the eyelids.

154
00:08:26.759 --> 00:08:31.686
Retinitis pigmentosa kills the rods first, so night blindness comes first.

155
00:08:31.686 --> 00:08:37.479
Macular degeneration loses central vision, and the dry kind has no effective treatment.

156
00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:40.942
Diabetes causes cataracts, glaucoma and retinopathy.

157
00:08:40.942 --> 00:08:46.002
Glaucoma is treated with beta blockers, conjunctivitis with chloramphenicol,

158
00:08:46.002 --> 00:08:50.331
astigmatism with toric lenses, and retinal detachment with laser.

159
00:08:50.781 --> 00:08:56.525
Ototoxic drugs, like gentamicin, furosemide, cisplatin, high-dose aspirin and quinine,

160
00:08:56.525 --> 00:08:59.197
kill hair cells: sensorineural deafness.

161
00:08:59.197 --> 00:09:02.803
High frequencies are heard at the base of the cochlea,

162
00:09:02.803 --> 00:09:05.408
low ones furthest from the oval window.

163
00:09:05.408 --> 00:09:08.882
Loud sound is felt as vibration by mechanoreceptors.

164
00:09:08.882 --> 00:09:14.759
The Doppler effect is a change in frequency for a moving observer, like a passing siren.

165
00:09:15.209 --> 00:09:18.062
The egg is fertilised in the fallopian tube.

166
00:09:18.062 --> 00:09:23.442
Her key calls the outer layer the zona radiata, and calcium lets the sperm through.

167
00:09:23.442 --> 00:09:29.277
Conception is most likely on days ten to seventeen, and ovulation kits detect the LH peak.

168
00:09:29.277 --> 00:09:34.268
The corpus luteum makes progesterone, oestrogen and relaxin for three months,

169
00:09:34.268 --> 00:09:39.519
then the placenta takes over; without a pregnancy it becomes the corpus albicans.

170
00:09:39.519 --> 00:09:41.529
A pregnancy test detects H C G.

171
00:09:41.529 --> 00:09:44.251
An embryo becomes a foetus at eight weeks.

172
00:09:44.251 --> 00:09:46.715
The mini pill never releases oxytocin.

173
00:09:46.715 --> 00:09:52.484
Breast cancer risks: little breastfeeding, early periods, late menopause, family history,

174
00:09:52.484 --> 00:09:53.716
and men get it too.
